      "font size" : 9.96,
      "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
      "content" : "5. Once we have received all initial and/or additional documentation requested, your Financial Aid staff will review your paperwork and the reported information on your FAFSA to ensure accuracy.",
      "kids" : [ ]
    }, {
      "type" : "list item",
      "pdfua_tag" : "LI",
      "page number" : 1,
      "bounding box" : [ 35.981, 395.861, 575.883, 422.454 ],
      "font" : "TimesNewRomanPS-BoldMT",
      "font size" : 9.96,
      "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
      "content" : "6. It is important to continue to check WebAdvisor and student email to see if any additional/supporting documentation is required.",
      "kids" : [ ]
    }, {
      "type" : "list item",
      "pdfua_tag" : "LI",
      "page number" : 1,
      "bounding box" : [ 35.981, 359.507, 576.002, 385.98 ],
      "font" : "TimesNewRomanPS-BoldMT",
      "font size" : 9.96,
      "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
      "content" : "7. Your Analyst will determine your eligibility by packaging and awarding your financial aid. You will then receive a revised Financial Aid Award email notification via your student email account.",
      "kids" : [ ]
    }, {
      "type" : "list item",
      "pdfua_tag" : "LI",
      "page number" : 1,
      "bounding box" : [ 35.981, 323.033, 576.032, 349.507 ],
      "font" : "TimesNewRomanPS-BoldMT",
      "font size" : 9.96,
      "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
      "content" : "8. You will receive your disbursement according to the processing deadline you meet. Please refer to the reverse for disbursement dates. DEADLINE DATES ARE SUBJECT TO CHANGE WITHOUT WARNING.",
      "kids" : [ ]
    }, {
      "type" : "list item",
      "pdfua_tag" : "LI",
      "page number" : 1,
      "bounding box" : [ 35.971, 273.363, 576.082, 313.033 ],
      "font" : "TimesNewRomanPS-BoldMT",
      "font size" : 9.96,
      "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
      "content" : "9. You will only be paid for classes you are actively attending. Remaining in all of your classes is critical to avoid repayment of funds received. If you receive payment for a class and drop, you may be required to repay a portion or the entire grant/ loan you received.",
      "kids" : [ ]
    }, {
      "type" : "list item",
      "pdfua_tag" : "LI",
      "page number" : 1,
